Cell[TextData[{
 "On the five-qubit code the transversal CNOT is not a gadget at all, which \
is section 11.4's argument run backwards: demanding it forces every generator \
to be ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],
 "-only or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],
 "-only, which is what being CSS means \[LongDash] and therefore why Steane \
EC, and the spliced-in correction of section 2, are CSS-only. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 " and CNOT generate the Clifford group, so the seven-qubit code performs the \
whole logical Clifford group transversally, each gate arriving conjugated per \
the sign above. Nothing outside that group is transversal on any code of this \
kind; that is chapter 13's problem, not this note's."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "6. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QECFaultTolerantCircuit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 " \[LongDash] spending all of it on a circuit"
}], "Section",ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition 10.6 says how to put the gadgets together. Take an ideal circuit \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],
 ", replace each of its qubits with a ",
 StyleBox["block",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", replace each of its locations with the corresponding gadget, and after \
every preparation, gate and storage gadget put an error correction gadget on \
each block involved \[LongDash] never after a measurement gadget, whose \
output is classical."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],

