  RowBox[{"7", ",", "1841", ",", "77", ",", "692"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[37]= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Seven locations become 1841 \[LongDash] counted on both sides as \
instructions ",
 StyleBox["plus waits", "TI"],
 ", which is what keeps the first ratio honest. Fourteen physical qubits per \
logical one: seven for the block and seven for its own correction workspace, \
one workspace per block so the corrections of a layer run in parallel instead \
of queueing. And nineteen and a quarter times the depth. Those are the \
numbers a fault-tolerance threshold has to beat, and they are why the subject \
is about ",
 StyleBox["rates", "TI"],
 " rather than counts."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the detail that makes this more than bookkeeping. Asked for a logical \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 ", the assembler emits a transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Union", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
   RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QECFaultTolerantCircuit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<S\>\"", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "steane"}], "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<GadgetInstructions\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Gate\>\""}], 
     "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", "\<\"Sdg\"\>", "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[38]= ",ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It never emits \"the transversal version of the gate it was asked for\" \
\[LongDash] it asks which word has the requested ",
 StyleBox["logical", "TI"],
 " action, which is section 5 doing work. A protocol assembled by name would \
compute the complex conjugate of the intended circuit and look perfectly \
healthy doing it: on the engine, assembled properly the encoded qubit ends in \
the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 " eigenstate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "_"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 ", and assembled by name in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 " eigenstate."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],

Cell["\<\
The classical side is tracked too. A measurement gadget's outcomes sit in a \
record otherwise full of error-correction syndromes, so a decoder has to be \
told which ones make the logical bit:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<measurements\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\"\<Measurements\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<logical bit of qubit 1\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\"\<Readouts\>\"", "]"}], "[", "1", "]"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<of qubit 2\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\"\<Readouts\>\"", "]"}], "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"measurements\"\>", "\[Rule]", "98"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"logical bit of qubit 1\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"86", ",", "88", ",", "90"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"of qubit 2\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"93", ",", "95", ",", "97"}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[39]= ",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three outcomes out of ninety-eight, being the support of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "_"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],
 " inside that block's own measurements."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],

Cell["\<\
And what the protocol is not, said by the object rather than left to the \
reader:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\"\<OpenAssumptions\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Spacings", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"Preparation of an encoded |0> uses the code's own encoder, which is \
not fault tolerant (Got26 Procedure 6.6); so do the ancillas of every error \
correction gadget. Fault-tolerant preparation is chapter 13 work.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"The gate gadgets are transversal, so the protocol is Clifford only. \
A universal set (Def 10.5) needs the constructions of chapter 13.\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Corrections are carried in the Pauli frame (sec. 12.5.2) rather \
than applied, so the emitted circuit has no classically conditioned \
instruction.\"\>"}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{1}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[40]= ",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The preparation gadget is the code's own encoder, and so are the ancillas \
of every correction \[LongDash] the same debt section 3 measured as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3", ",", "4"}], "}"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 ". The gate gadgets are transversal, so the gate set is Clifford: Definition \
10.5 asks for a ",
 StyleBox["universal", "TI"],
 " set, and a circuit with a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " in it is refused rather than approximated. And corrections stay in the \
Pauli frame, so nothing in the emitted circuit is classically conditioned \
\[LongDash] which is what real experiments do, and one fewer location that \
can fail."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],

Cell["7. Verified ancillas \[LongDash] the debt, paid", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every gadget above rests on encoded ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "0"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "+"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],
 " blocks made by the code's own encoder, and one fault in that encoder can \
spread over several qubits. Section 13.1.2 makes them fault tolerant by ",
 StyleBox["checking one copy against another",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " (fig. 13.3): encode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"|", "0"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],
 " twice, apply a transversal CNOT from the copy to be kept into the other, \
measure the other, and keep the copy only if the comparison sees nothing. Bit \
flips on the kept copy are copied into the checker and seen there; so are \
faults in the checker's own encoder."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\"Sees nothing\" is a set of parities, not all zeros: the checker's \
outcomes are a random codeword, so the test is that its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],
 "-type checks and its logical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],
 " all read zero. The gadget carries those parities as ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<HeraldChecks\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],
 ", one block of rows per verified ancilla:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ecv", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QECErrorCorrection", "[", 
    RowBox[{"steane", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Ancilla\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Verified\>\""}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{"ecv", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Ancilla\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Qubits\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<Verifications\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<InstructionCount\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<Depth\>\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"Ancilla\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Verified\"\>"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Qubits\"\>", "\[Rule]", "35"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Verifications\"\>", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"InstructionCount\"\>", "\[Rule]", "146"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Depth\"\>", "\[Rule]", "13"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[41]= ",ExpressionUUID->"6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Four ancilla blocks instead of one \[LongDash] a kept copy and a checker \
for each half, prepared side by side so the data waits for none of them. The \
encoder is the CSS one of fig. 14.8a, three Hadamards and nine CNOTs instead \
of the 25 gates of the general construction. And the phase errors the \
comparison does not look at are harmless on this code for the book's reason: \
the Hamming code is perfect, so every phase-error syndrome is a single phase \
error, and on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"|", "0"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],
 " a logical phase error is no error."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell["\<\
The claim is checked, not assumed. Every single fault in the gadget, in every \
run the comparison accepts, with the gadget's own correction applied, and the \
residual weighed modulo the stabilizer:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<verified\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ecv", "[", "\"\<ResidualWeights\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<bare encoder\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QECErrorCorrection", "[", "steane", "]"}], 
     "[", "\"\<ResidualWeights\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"verified\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"Preparation\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Verification\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Interaction\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Waits\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"bare encoder\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"Preparation\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Interaction\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Waits\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], 
     "\[RightAssociation]"}]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[42]= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the bare encoder one fault can leave three errors \[LongDash] on a \
distance-3 code, a logical error. Verified, no fault anywhere leaves more \
than one. That is the chapter-13 property, and with it the open assumption of \
sections 3 and 6 becomes a post-selection whose cost is counted below. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QECFaultTolerantCircuit", "[", 
   RowBox[{"circuit", ",", " ", "code", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Ancilla\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Verified\>\""}]}], "]"}]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],
 " builds the whole of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],
 " this way, its preparation gadgets included."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "8. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QECExtendedRectangle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],
 " \[LongDash] the proof, one piece at a time"
}], "Section",ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The threshold theorem is proved one piece of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],
 " at a time. An ",
 StyleBox["extended rectangle",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a gadget with the error-correction gadgets right before and right after \
it (Def 14.2). It is ",
 StyleBox["good", "TI"],
 " if it holds at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],
 " faults (Def 14.4), and a good exRec is ",
 StyleBox["correct", "TI"],
 " \[LongDash] it does to the encoded state what the ideal location does \
(Theorem 14.1). So a computation can only go wrong where an exRec is bad, and \
a union bound over its sets of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 " locations bounds the chance of that (eq. 14.29), divided by the acceptance \
of each post-selected ancilla (eq. 14.33):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Pr", 
     RowBox[{"(", "bad", ")"}]}], "\[LessEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
      "Binomial"], " ", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "-", 
         StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], ")"}], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]]}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],
 " the exRec's locations, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],
 " the chance of a fault in one preparation attempt, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],
 " the post-selections. The CNOT exRec of the 7-qubit code, from this layer's \
own circuit:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rect", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QECExtendedRectangle", "[", 
    RowBox[{"steane", ",", " ", "\"\<CNOT\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<parts\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<Parts\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<locations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<LocationCounts\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<A\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<Locations\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<k\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<Verifications\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Q / p\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<PreparationLocations\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"parts\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"LeadingEC\"\>", "\[Rule]", "292"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Gate\"\>", "\[Rule]", "7"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"TrailingEC\"\>", "\[Rule]", "292"}]}], 
     "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"locations\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"Measurement\"\>", "\[Rule]", "112"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"OneQubitGate\"\>", "\[Rule]", "104"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Preparation\"\>", "\[Rule]", "112"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"TwoQubitGate\"\>", "\[Rule]", "263"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Wait\"\>", "\[Rule]", "188"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}],
    ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"A\"\>", "\[Rule]", "779"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"k\"\>", "\[Rule]", "8"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Q / p\"\>", "\[Rule]", "58"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[43]= ",ExpressionUUID->"0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Section 14.5.3 counts the same exRec of its own circuit: 263 CNOTs, 112 \
preparations, 112 measurements and 8 post-selections \[LongDash] ",
 StyleBox["the same",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". It has 112 one-qubit gates to our 104 because it budgets two Pauli \
corrections per EC, which here stay in the Pauli frame. It has 136 waits to \
our 188, because its circuit is laid out by hand and ours by an ASAP \
schedule; a wait is counted here as the book counts it, a qubit holding a \
state through a step in which nothing touches it. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "735"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 " there and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["779", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],
 " here, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "63", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 " there and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"58", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],
 " here."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bound gives a threshold: if every exRec at one level fails with \
probability at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], ")"}], "<", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],
 ", the next level of concatenation squares the ratio, so the threshold is at \
least the fixed point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],
 " of the worst exRec (eq. 14.63). With the book's counts that is its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3.6", "\[Cross]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "6"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],
 "; with ours:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", " ", "@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "Wolfram`QuantumFramework`QEC`PackageScope`concatenationThreshold", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"735", ",", " ", "63", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1"}],
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<ThresholdBound\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"3.700296840809644`*^-6", ",", "3.294950566643438`*^-6"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[44]= ",ExpressionUUID->"0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Malignant sets",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " are the better count. A set of locations is ",
 StyleBox["malignant", "TI"],
 " if some choice of Pauli errors on it, in a run the heralds accept, makes \
the exRec incorrect, and ",
 StyleBox["benign", "TI"],
 " otherwise (Def 14.7). The union bound charges every pair as fatal; most \
are not. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MalignantPairs\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],
 " counts the ones that are, by trying every Pauli on every pair: each \
single-qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],
 " at each place is propagated once and kept as a handful of integers \
\[LongDash] herald parities, syndromes, frames \[LongDash] so a pair is an \
XOR and the decoders are table lookups. The input to the exRec can be taken \
to be a perfect codeword, and that is an argument, not a shortcut: the \
leading EC leaves a residual whose syndrome does not depend on what came in, \
and the logical part of what came in passes through both sides of the \
comparison alike."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<singles\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<MalignantSingles\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<pairs\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<MalignantPairs\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<of\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"rect", "[", "\"\<Locations\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"singles\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"pairs\"\>", "\[Rule]", "67051"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"of\"\>", "\[Rule]", "303031"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[45]= ",ExpressionUUID->"7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "No single location is malignant \[LongDash] Theorem 14.1, checked on this \
circuit, and with the bare encoder it fails (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QECExtendedRectangle", "[", 
    RowBox[{"steane", ",", " ", "\"\<H\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Ancilla\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Encoder\>\""}]}], "]"}], 
   "[", "\"\<MalignantSingles\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],
 " is 42). Of the 303 031 pairs, 67 051 are malignant, about one in four."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell["\<\
The threshold with malignant pairs counted, and every triple still charged as \
fatal (eq. 14.32), over all the exRecs of the protocol:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"thc", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QECThreshold", "[", 
    RowBox[{"steane", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Method\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Concatenation\>\""}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<bound\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"N", "[", 
     RowBox[{"thc", "[", "\"\<Value\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<worst\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"thc", "[", "\"\<Worst\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<per exRec\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"N", "[", "#FixedPoint", "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"thc", "[", "\"\<ExtendedRectangles\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[46]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"bound\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.000014565203727264702`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"worst\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"CNOT\"\>"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"per exRec\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"Preparation\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.0002536682936765879`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Measurement\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.0007529214199803766`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Wait\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.000043596612293595065`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"H\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.00003757356582429146`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"S\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.00003184404018745143`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"CNOT\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.000014565203727264702`"}]}], 
     "\[RightAssociation]"}]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[46]= ",ExpressionUUID->"4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1.46", "\[Cross]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],
 ", against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3.3", "\[Cross]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "6"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],
 " from bad sets. The book reaches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2.7", "\[Cross]", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 " for its protocol with malignant counting ",
 StyleBox["and", "TI"],
 " circuit optimizations; the extra waits of an ASAP layout, and the triples \
still charged in full, are where the remaining factor lies."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"thc", "[", "\"\<Caveats\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[47]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"This is a lower bound on the threshold of concatenating this \
one fault-tolerant protocol (Got26 Def 14.10), not an estimate of it, under \
adversarial noise at one rate p for every kind of location.\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Pairs of locations are counted as fatal only if some Pauli \
errors on them make the exRec incorrect in an accepted run (Def 14.7); every \
triple is still counted as fatal (eq. 14.32).\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"It comes from the worst extended rectangle, the CNOT one, \
through eps(p) = p (eq. 14.63).\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"The protocol is this layer's circuit -- Steane EC with verified \
ancillas, transversal Clifford gates -- laid out by an ASAP schedule; the \
book's hand-laid circuit has fewer waits, and a different circuit has a \
different bound.\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Clifford gates only: \\\"GateSet\\\" -> \\\"Universal\\\" adds \
the pi/8 exRec, which makes the protocol universal and lowers the \
bound.\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[47]= ",ExpressionUUID->"10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is a lower bound three ways over \[LongDash] adversarial errors, triples \
all charged, one particular circuit \[LongDash] and it is meant to be read as \
one. The same section of the book sets its own bounds of this kind next to \
the roughly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"0.7", "%"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],
 " that simulations give for the surface code (sec. 14.7.4): a proof that a \
threshold exists is not an estimate of where it is."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "9. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "8"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],
 " gate, and what it all costs"
}], "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Transversal gates are Clifford, and the Clifford group is not universal: \
the missing gate is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "8"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 ". It is done without a transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],
 " at all (sec. 13.3): prepare an encoded ",
 StyleBox["magic state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"|", "+"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 ", check it, and spend it. Spending it is fig. 13.7 \[LongDash] a \
transversal CNOT from the magic block into the data, a transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 " measurement of the data, and on outcome 1 a Clifford correction \
\[LongDash] so the injection uses only gates the protocol already has."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The magic state is made by the CSS encoder with one more wire (fig. 14.8b): \
a qubit carrying a representative of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "_"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],
 " is put in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"|", "+"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],
 " and fanned out. Four Hadamards, one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 ", eleven CNOTs \[LongDash] the book's counts \[LongDash] and on state \
vectors the result is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"|", "+"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],
 ". It is not fault tolerant, so it is ",
 StyleBox["tested",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": the magic state is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 " eigenstate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 ", a Clifford up to phase, which a verified cat state can measure (fig. \
14.9). On this code the transversal test operator certifies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"|", "+"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],
 " rather than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"|", "+"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 " \[LongDash] the transversal map conjugates, as transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],
 " is logical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],
 " \[LongDash] so the protocol injects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 " costs one more Clifford. On outcome 1 the correction is a transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],
 ", kept in the frame, then a transversal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],
 "; both branches were checked on state vectors."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QECExtendedRectangle", "[", 
    RowBox[{"steane", ",", " ", "\"\<T\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<parts\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rT", "[", "\"\<Parts\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<locations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rT", "[", "\"\<LocationCounts\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<magic attempt\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rT", "[", "\"\<MagicPreparationLocations\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<malignant pairs\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rT", "[", "\"\<MalignantPairs\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
