Cell["\<\
Three levels already cost over a hundred million physical locations per \
logical one, which is the book's own conclusion: the threshold theorem is a \
feasibility result, and the codes that are practical (chapter 17) are \
practical because their overhead is far smaller.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],

Cell["The six, side by side", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],

